<p>Summoned via PM.</p>
<p>I'm afraid this seems rather cliche on the face of it - trapping people in a video game isn't the most ubiquitous idea in the world, but it's not particularly original and it's rather overdone. It's not something I find particularly interesting nor particularly unique - it's a thing that does a thing, and worse still, that thing is essentially just violence. Whilst not directly killing people, it functionally does as much and that's the kind of thing we've seen a lot of onsite.</p>
<p>However, it's generally more important that you do something interesting with an anomaly than anything else. Currently, you haven't really got a story, and that's your biggest issue. You've got more detailed description of the mechanics of the anomaly, but not an actual narrative or story. You need to tell a story in your article - that's was SCPs really are, vehicles for storytelling, so it's really the most important bit. The crucial question is, what's the story here?</p>

