<p>Hi Costansin,</p>
<p>I've read your revised concept on the forums. It's definitely more detailed in terms of the discovery and test logs on the laptop. You've described how the scp works in alot of detail, but we still don't understand <em>why</em> it's doing this and why is it choosing its victims at random. Okay, so they watch a video that's &quot;intriguing&quot; to them? So what? It's goal is simply to get as many victims as possible?</p>
<p>Consider revising the way the laptop picks / chooses its victims, especially since you're going for a mind-affecting anomaly. For example, could it be that the laptop allows a user to chat with a dead loved one from his/her past? This is a more natural way of engaging a user without having to affect his/her mind. An alternative would be for the previous user (now a prisoner in the laptop) to communicate with the new victim in order to trick him/her to take their place. You see where I'm going with this? Your anomalous effects should be connected in some way. Instead, they still seem entirely random.</p>

							</div>

								
					
