<p>Hi caspian2,</p>
<p>It is my fault for not explaining thoroughly enough. The reason I decided to use thumbnails that can change depending on what the viewer finds intriguing is because I want to relate this to a concept that is seen on real video-sharing websites which is clickbait, where the thumbnails are often misleading or anticlimactic.</p>
<p>Your advice is again extremely helpful and I think I can incorporate it into my SCP. For example, with the idea of a dead loved one from his/her past, if the viewer deeply misses a dead loved one, than the SCP could create a thumbnail that seemingly provides closure for the viewer. Of course, it is a trap and the viewer becomes another victim.</p>
<p>For your other question of why is it doing this, I have come up with an idea that again relates to the concept of clickbait. Most people who use clickbait thumbnails usually are trying to make money. So, to incorporate this into the SCP, the SCP is kidnapping people using its anomalous effects and is selling them on the black market. At some point, the SCP Foundation intervenes and manages to rescue a victim. The SCP Foundation realizes that there has to be a mastermind behind this SCP, however the victim they save is severely injured and has been administered with amnestics.</p>
<p>Once again, I greatly appreciate all the advice and help you have given me so far. Please offer more advice that you think I may need.</p>

